736e4cd3799cfe12f26cdce1350d32e4088d07823e581ee3a95a26fb8a4e167c,ott2019,sea_level_indicator,"Moho, Puno, Perú",page_11_feature_1,-15.3549442,-69.4058564,inferred_text,10000.0,3977.0,MSL,SRTM15+V2,submerged_beach,page OCR extracted from figure/table/map block,null,null,other,"Pleistocene terrace formation, Quaternary rock uplift rates and geodynamics of the Hellenic Subduction Zone revealed from dating of paleoshorelines on Crete, Greece","Moho, Puno, Perú","Pleistocene terrace formation, Quaternary rock uplift rates and geodynamics of the Hellenic Subduction Zone revealed from dating of paleoshorelines on Crete, Greece",https://doi.org/10.1016/j.epsl.2019.115757,0.7,"Extracted from page OCR block on page 11 with cue 'Fig. 9. Schematic interpretation of kinematics and uplift patterns for the Central Hellenic orogenic wedge, with individ' from source 'mineru_image'. Place name geocoded from query 'Moho'.","{""page"": ""11"", ""figure"": ""Fig. 9. Schematic interpretation of kinematics and uplift patterns for the Central Hellenic orogenic wedge, with individ"", ""table"": null, ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""Fig. 9. Schematic interpretation of kinematics and uplift patterns for the Central Hellenic orogenic wedge, with individual interpretations of: (a) Western Crete and (b) Eastern Crete. In both sections, frontal accretion of sediments takes place in the vicinity of the Mediterranean Ridge; To the north, under the island of Crete, structural underplating of sediment leads to long wavelength, secular uplift. The uplift signal is localized by the geometry of the upper plate with underplating and uplift confined to trenchward and around the of the contact between the upper plate Moho and the top of the lower plate. The interior of the upper plate is extending in the Cretan Sea, and crustal thinning and subsidence affect parts of the north coast of Crete. text_image images/0caa64f031c236909fa059""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": 