033d6202004f0e0a4b7371b4bbbbbb3ce0639940f4e9e22d1c94897406ff7eb7,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,"San Julian Pa 122, Pa 123, beach ridge - Pa 122, Pa 123, beach ridge",RSL_562@row751,-49.327193,-67.809105,reported,0.0,5.09,MSL,reported,raised_beach,Beach ridge,"[3.505, 4.095]",119.0,esr,"Beach ridge; Regressive beach ridge deposit, composed of grain supported gravel. There are two shell rich layers, which were interpreted to be in-situ. The lower shell rich layer (labeled Pa 123) is at the base of the deposit, while the second layer (labeled Pa 122) is about 0.8 m above the base. The total thickness of the deposit is about 1.5 m. Underlying the beach ridge deposit is a beach deposit. There is a thin layer of colluvium (<0.1 m) overlying the beach ridge deposit. Ice wedge pseudomorphs were observed at this location, indicating that they deposited prior to a period of cold climatic conditions.","San Julian Pa 122, Pa 123, beach ridge, Pa 122, Pa 123, beach ridge, Santa Cruz, Argentina","Schellmann, 1998 Schellmann and Radtke, 1997 Schellmann and Radtke, 1999 Schellmann and Radtke, 2000 Gowan et al., 2021",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,0.955,"WALIS quality RSL=2, age=3. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: K-2669. Analysis ID: SC89-052-001. WALIS ESR ID: 86. Record Created by: Evan Gowan. Last Update: 2020-05-12 06:00:55.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_562@row751"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_562: Sea Level Indicator; Beach ridge; elevation 8.9 m; paleo RSL 5.09 m; dating ESR.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 8.9, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 2.89}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 5.09, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""WALIS