8cedb5c41af4b950c1052fbb9de7cc29d5c78a7999c7688db94d7532323ec6fa,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,São Bento - Touros São Bento outcrop - São Bento outcrop,RSL_144@row1240,-5.056,-36.043,reported,0.0,19.88,MSL,reported,marine_terrace,Marine Terrace,"[-2.125, 2.3449999999999998]",117.0,luminescence,"Marine Terrace; The marine terrace deposits is preserved for about 120 km along mainly the E-W-trending coast. The most conspicuous outcrops are more than 2 km long and are situated between São Bento and Touros. Marine terraces, which are 1-10 m in altitude between São Bento and Touros, rise to a maximum of 20 m asl to the north of Zumbi. Deposits are mainly made up of medium- to coarse-grained sand-stones. The basal part pf the deposit is composed of coarse to conglomeratic, tabular and trough cross-bedded sandstone. Herring-bone cross-bedded sandstone occurs in places. On the top of the deposit is a swash cross-bedded sandstone, where Ophimorpha nodosa burrows that form at the beach sub-environment are common.","São Bento - Touros São Bento outcrop, São Bento outcrop, Rio Grande do Norte, Brazil","Barreto et al., 2002 Rubio-Sandoval et al., 2021 Suguio et al., 2005",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,0.955,"WALIS quality RSL=3, age=2. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: 32-98. Analysis ID: BA02-001-001. WALIS LUM ID: 36. Record Created by: Karla Zurisadai Rubio Sandoval. Last Update: 2021-02-06 16:04:03.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_144@row1240"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_144: Sea Level Indicator; Marine Terrace; elevation 20.0 m; paleo RSL 19.88 m; dating Luminescence.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 20.0, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 2.99}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": 