37cc21789e6991b39e5edeb1ac4fe2a217b39d76becfb97d057e58e7408ea7cf,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,São Bento - Touros Touros outcrop - Touros outcrop,RSL_163@row1250,-5.213,-35.433,reported,69.73209504458971,19.99,MSL,reported,marine_terrace,Marine Terrace,"[-2.285, 2.285]",117.0,luminescence,"Marine Terrace; The marine terrace deposits is preserved for about 120 km along mainly the E-W-trending coast. The most conspicuous outcrops are more than 2 km long and are situated between São Bento and Touros. Marine terraces, which are 1-10 m in altitude between São Bento and Touros, rise to a maximum of 20 m asl to the north of Zumbi. Deposits are mainly made up of medium- to coarse-grained sand-stones. The basal part pf the deposit is composed of coarse to conglomeratic, tabular and trough cross-bedded sandstone. Herring-bone cross-bedded sandstone occurs in places. On the top of the deposit is a swash cross-bedded sandstone, where Ophimorpha nodosa burrows that form at the beach sub-environment are common.","São Bento - Touros Touros outcrop, Touros outcrop, Rio Grande do Norte, Brazil","Barreto et al., 2002 Rubio-Sandoval et al., 2021 Suguio et al., 2005",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,0.98,"WALIS quality RSL=3, age=3. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: 32-98. Analysis ID: BA02-001-001. WALIS LUM ID: 36. Record Created by: Karla Zurisadai Rubio Sandoval. Last Update: 2020-02-24 04:24:34.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_163@row1250"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_163: Sea Level Indicator; Marine Terrace; elevation 20.0 m; paleo RSL 19.99 m; dating Luminescence.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 20.0, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 3.03}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""deri