c619bd7098733a4c86f8ddea7645858d322519f1531dfd7395be861b2d33c68c,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,North coast of East Timor Timor-Hau section (MIS 5e) - Timor-Hau section (MIS 5e),RSL_3618@row2999,-8.52255,125.716005,reported,0.0,10.0,MSL,reported,coral_reef,Coral reef terrace (general definition),"[-0.9550000000000001, -0.905]",142.0,u_series,"Coral reef terrace (general definition); Hau Section: ""Adjacent to the road 4 km east of the hamlet of Hau near Dili, there is a raised reef, capped by fluvial fan gravels. Shallow-water fringing reef facies pass upward into beach beds and wedge out laterally in bedrock, 10 m above LWL. A basal conglomerate overlies bedrock. No higher reefs exist at this place, but a second outcrop of reef occurs below the road toward the eastern end of the beach.""","North coast of East Timor Timor-Hau section (MIS 5e), Timor-Hau section (MIS 5e), N/A, East Timor","Chappell and Veeh, 1978 Maxwell et al., 2021",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=5, age=4. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=Yes. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: TM74-2. Analysis ID: CH78-015-001. WALIS U-series ID: 2890. Record Created by: Kathrine Maxwell. Last Update: 2021-02-17 13:52:31.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_3618@row2999"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_3618: Sea Level Indicator; Coral reef terrace (general definition); elevation 9.07 m; paleo RSL 10.0 m; dating U-Series.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 9.07, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 0.4}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 10.0, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""WALIS Paleo RSL used as LITTORAL analytical elevation when available; measured indicator elevation preserved as reported observatio