04a680e9aee933d369a373291fd729d053de6a583ff6c4adbac3be7aa50c6252,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,North coast of East Timor Timor-Baucau section (MIS 5c) - Timor-Baucau section (MIS 5c),RSL_3620@row3002,-8.439155,126.461676,reported,0.0,43.0,MSL,reported,coral_reef,Coral reef terrace (general definition),"[-0.9550000000000001, -0.905]",100.0,u_series,"Coral reef terrace (general definition); Baucau Beach Area: Extensive reef limestones around Baucau rise from sea level to about 500 m in a series of major terraces, the crests and fronts of which are broken by gravity slides on the underlying Tertiary shales. These were named the ""Baucau Limestone"" by Audley- Charles (1968), who mapped correlative reef limestone extensively toward the eastern tip of the island. A reef and associated terrace at 43m above LWL that occur 0.5 km east of the carpark appear to be in place. This well-defined terrace is a horizontal reef flat and stands seaward of a higher terrace which is about 65 to 70 m above LWL. Stratigraphic relationships are obscured by dense secondary bush. Two samples from beneath the 43-m crest gave ages, judged reliable, of 100,000 and 108,000 yr B.P.","North coast of East Timor Timor-Baucau section (MIS 5c), Timor-Baucau section (MIS 5c), N/A, East Timor","Chappell and Veeh, 1978 Maxwell et al., 2021",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=5, age=4. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=Yes. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: TM74-10. Analysis ID: CH78-020-001. WALIS U-series ID: 2895. Record Created by: Kathrine Maxwell. Last Update: 2021-02-17 14:05:49.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_3620@row3002"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_3620: Sea Level Indicator; Coral reef terrace (general definition); elevation 42.07 m; paleo RSL 43.0 m; dating U-Series.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 42.07, ""reported_depth_m""