eaa2552988cb129d7f7bc8944d068a4e8b363adf0e35b14074774db7c8e2c83a,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,North coast of East Timor Terraces 50 km East of Baucau (Lautem area) (MIS 5a) - Terraces 50 km East of Baucau (Lautem area) (MIS 5a),RSL_3621@row3005,-8.363021,126.904672,reported,0.0,26.0,MSL,reported,coral_reef,Coral reef terrace (general definition),"[-0.9550000000000001, -0.905]",78.0,u_series,"Coral reef terrace (general definition); ""Terraces 50 km East of Baucau (Lautem area): Good sections exist through extensive fluviatile terraces and pass laterally into the equivalent of the Baucau limestone around Lautem (mapped by Audley-Charles, 1968). The reefs are thin and are completely recrystallized above the lowest terrace, which has the inner margin of fringing reef 26 m above LWL. The terrace is correlated with MIS 5a, and the 40-m height of the inner margin of the next highest reef wedge is consistent with MIS 5c. The next terrace above is very broad and entirely fluviatile, and its underlying beds pass beneath the 26-m and 40-m reef wedges. This can be correlated with MIS 5e.","North coast of East Timor Terraces 50 km East of Baucau (Lautem area) (MIS 5a), Terraces 50 km East of Baucau (Lautem area) (MIS 5a), N/A, East Timor","Chappell and Veeh, 1978 Maxwell et al., 2021",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=5, age=4. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=Yes. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: TM74-14. Analysis ID: CH78-023-001. WALIS U-series ID: 2898. Record Created by: Kathrine Maxwell. Last Update: 2021-02-17 14:12:12.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_3621@row3005"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_3621: Sea Level Indicator; Coral reef terrace (general definition); elevation 25.07 m; paleo RSL 26.0 m; dating U-Series.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 25.07, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": "