4e56cc22b0e1e860c6bcb883f062b17baea20c5bb17d716086f01fb46fcfc88d,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,North coast of East Timor Subau - Manatuto (Manatuto TI) - MIS 5e? - Subau - Manatuto (Manatuto TI) - MIS 5e?,RSL_3647@row3007,-8.489722,125.988486,reported,0.2686177265832199,6.74,MSL,reported,coral_reef,Coral reef terrace (general definition),"[-1.195, -0.885]",146.703,u_series,"Coral reef terrace (general definition); Elevation of dated sample taken at the mid-platform. The modern beach with an inner margin at c. 10 m asl and composed of beach rock that is exposed above high tide and consists of poorly sorted, polymictic, 50:50 matrix to clast ratio, with no coral. The terrace also cuts into a 2 meter thick unit of coralline limestone. The coralline limestone grades into a non-coralline limestone unit. In this profile, the terraces are flat and extend along the coast for nearly 2.5 km. The west terraces are truncated, possibly due to a fault that juxtaposes the coral terraces with metamorphosed bedrock. The lower terraces can be followed eastward until obliterated by fluvial deposits. The terraces strike roughly NW-SE, which mimics the local modern coastline. Seven terraces are identified in the field and from aerial photos, but lack well defined notches.","North coast of East Timor Subau - Manatuto (Manatuto TI) - MIS 5e?, Subau - Manatuto (Manatuto TI) - MIS 5e?, N/A, East Timor","Cox, 2009 Maxwell et al., 2021",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=5, age=3. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=N/A. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: Man-35. Analysis ID: CO09-014-001. WALIS U-series ID: 2966. Record Created by: Kathrine Maxwell. Last Update: 2021-02-28 13:58:16.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_3647@row3007"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_3647: Sea Level Indicator; Coral reef terrace (general definition); elevation 5.7 m; paleo RSL 6.74 m; dating U-Series.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 5.7, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 0.52}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 6.74, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""WALIS Paleo RSL used as LITTORAL analytical elevation when available; measured indicator elevation preserved as reported observation.""}","[{""method"": ""u_series"", ""relation"": ""equal"", ""age_ka"": 146.703, ""uncertainty_ka"": 1.0874, ""material"": ""Coral"", ""notes"": ""WALIS reported age.""}]",6.74,6.74,6.74,6.74
37e183e827b42d0a8bfcb7fe02dc352fd2c21a083120b243804bb569158d5a8f,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,North coast of East Timor Manatuto-Baucau (Liarua TI) - MIS 5e? - Manatuto-Baucau (Liarua TI) - MIS 5e?,RSL_3649@row3009,-8.415547,126.414244,reported,0.0,6.94,MSL,reported,coral_reef,Coral reef terrace (general definition),"[-1.195, -0.885]",136.689,u_series,"Coral reef terrace (general definition); Elevation of dated sample at 6m. Multiple benches occur within this terrace. Inner margins occur at 8 m, 14 m, 16 m and 20 m, but are not continuous or commonly join one another, as evident by double notches. The terrace reaches a maximum inland margin c. 26 m asl; although, this margin can also be as low as 8 m asl due to the waning traces of subterraces. Surfaces are composed of pink cemented beach sediment and loose basalt pebbles. Near the notch are large boulders representing blocks of Terrace II that have fallen onto Terrace I.","North coast of East Timor Manatuto-Baucau (Liarua TI) - MIS 5e?, Manatuto-Baucau (Liarua TI) - MIS 5e?, N/A, East Timor","Cox, 2009 Maxwell et al., 2021",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=5, age=4. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=N/A. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: Lia-38. Analysis ID: CO09-001-001. WALIS U-series ID: 2959. Record Created by: Kathrine Maxwell. Last Update: 2021-02-28 14:01:28.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_3649@row3009"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_3649: Sea Level Indicator; Coral reef terrace (general definition); elevation 5.9 m; paleo RSL 6.94 m; dating U-Series.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 5.9, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 0.52}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 6.94, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivati