bf7ea068388184493c3dbff8678de35c37a0f9b970c9a14ccd6f0119cc53122f,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,Du Guesclin Top of a wave-cut platform - Top of a wave-cut platform,RSL_3659@row3258,48.689846,-1.900555,reported,0.0,5.89,unknown,reported,marine_terrace,Marine Terrace,"[-0.6000000000000001, 4.82]",90.0,luminescence,"Marine Terrace; The cross-section at Du Guesclin is exposed on top of a wave-cut platform, at a height of 8 m NGF. To simplify the description, the cross-section is divided into several units, from the base upwards. The sediment cover starts with some marine pebbles (not always present). Above these pebbles, unit A is a mixture of sand and angular gravels of migmatite with diferent thin layers of about 1 cm deep. Unit B is a layer of coarse sand, without any visible structure. Units C and D display the same stratigraphic pattern of a layer of £at, subangular small pebbles (3^5-cm-long axis), directly covered by coarse- to medium-grained sand.","Du Guesclin Top of a wave-cut platform, Top of a wave-cut platform, Bretagne, France","Regnauld et al., 2003",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,0.955,"WALIS quality RSL=4, age=1. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: 129. Analysis ID: RE03-003-001. WALIS LUM ID: 309. Record Created by: Víctor Cartelle. Last Update: 2021-02-13 00:27:20.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_3659@row3258"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_3659: Sea Level Indicator; Marine Terrace; elevation 8.0 m; paleo RSL 5.89 m; dating Luminescence.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 8.0, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""NGF"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 2.88}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 5.89, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""WALIS Paleo RSL used as LITTORAL analytical elevation when av