66ba6963e86457e5b4e33f5b001173a040bbfda3da1c1937b72abb03eb07d08d,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,Lepe-Stone Point Site Lepe. Site TP7 Top of unit 2d - Lepe. Site TP7 Top of unit 2d,RSL_3760@row3405,50.784189,-1.35216,reported,0.03191797098432821,-2.55,MSL,reported,estuarine_sediment,Shallow or intertidal marine fauna,"[0.10000000000000009, 2.0]",141.0,luminescence,"Shallow or intertidal marine fauna; Lepe Unit 2d, close to top. Age: pollen zone IpIIb. Unit 2d is a tiff grey clay with shells. In the upper parts of Unit 2d the dominant foraminifera are Ammonia aberdoveyensis, A. limnetes and Elphidium waddense, all of which indicate brackish conditions, in a tidal river or estuary, with E. waddense and the agglutinating saltmarsh species, Trochammina inflata indicating low saltmarsh. The dominant ostracod is Cyprideis torosa. The environment represented in the upper parts of Unit 2d is interpreted as an area of low saltmarsh, cut by creeks.","Lepe-Stone Point Site Lepe. Site TP7 Top of unit 2d, Lepe. Site TP7 Top of unit 2d, Hampshire, Great Britain (UK)","Briant et al., 2019 Briant et al., 2006",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,0.955,"WALIS quality RSL=4, age=1. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: LEPE03-03. Analysis ID: BR06-018-001. WALIS LUM ID: 372. Record Created by: Víctor Cartelle. Last Update: 2021-10-14 13:49:37.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_3760@row3405"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_3760: Sea Level Indicator; Shallow or intertidal marine fauna; elevation -1.5 m; paleo RSL -2.55 m; dating Luminescence.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": -1.5, ""reported_depth_m"": 1.5, ""reported_datum"": ""OD (Ordnance Datum Newlyn)"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 1.07}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": -2.55, ""derived_depth_m"": null, 