00b35b19ea2b7ba8a64f3116b2c48d2576ce158eee5d3abc1a0fae76d2f5d72f,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,Bacon Hole Cave 'Shelly sand' storm beach - 'Shelly sand' storm beach,RSL_4007@row3426,51.561947,-4.078282,reported,0.005159418654775452,8.06,MSL,reported,raised_beach,Beach swash deposit,"[3.9400000000000004, 4.94]",125.0,u_series,"Beach swash deposit; Sequence of deposits overlaying limestone basement. 'Basal pebbles' (littoral, coarse, lag deposit), overlain by 'coarse grey sands' well sorted, finely bedded of aeolian origin, overlain by 'coarse orange sands' similar to the underlying sands but containing locally derived angular limestone clasts and silts, overlain by 'sandy-breccio-conglomerate' well bedded pebbles and shingles thinning to shingle and coarse sand with marine shell debris and interpreted as a storm beach, overlain by 'sandy cave earth' with large limestone clasts in a heterogenous matric with shelly lenses, overlain by shelly sands of marine shell debris with some limestone clasts. The shelly sand deposit, which is dated with u-series, is taken to be indicative of a beach ridge / beach swash deposit","Bacon Hole Cave 'Shelly sand' storm beach, 'Shelly sand' storm beach, Vale of Glamorgan, Great Britain (UK)","Sutcliffe et al., 1987 Stringer et al., 1986",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=3, age=4. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=N/A. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS corrected U-Series speleothem age. Originally reported ID: 1981-212:02. Analysis ID: ST86-003-002. WALIS U-series ID: 3164. Record Created by: Rob Barnett. Last Update: 2021-05-28 12:05:55.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_4007@row3426"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_4007: Sea Level Indicator; Beach swash deposit; elevation 12.5 m; paleo RSL 8.06 m; dating U-Series.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 12.5, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""OD (Ordn