44daca65179abf6b43ec4905d37c6e84c9cc3627c34046f0fb20b3d9490a1d90,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,Morton,RSL_4063@row3431,52.95709,0.956835,reported,0.0,1.56,MSL,reported,raised_beach,Beach swash deposit,"[0.04999999999999993, 1.83]",191.0,luminescence,"Beach swash deposit; A sequence of deposits (overlying a basal till) largely made up of very well-sorted, predominantly subangular and subrounded fine quartz sands, with subsidiary feldspar and aragonite. The sands are characterized by approximately parallel bedding which dips seawards at low angles. This may represent swash cross-stratification typical of the swash zone of the foreshore. The presence of occasional gravels within the sands is also characteristic of deposits from this environment. The marginal marine origin of these units is supported by their very well-sorted particle-size distribution. The occurrence of aragonite within the mineral assemblage of sample 2 is suggestive of the presence of fragments of marine shell in the sands, although it is possible that the shells may have been reworked from older marine deposits.","Morton, Norfolk, Great Britain (UK)",Gale 1988 Hoare 2009 JQS,https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=3, age=4. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: SA-Morst-4. Analysis ID: 001. WALIS LUM ID: 504. Record Created by: Natasha Barlow. Last Update: 2021-06-21 15:14:53.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_4063@row3431"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_4063: Sea Level Indicator; Beach swash deposit; elevation 2.5 m; paleo RSL 1.56 m; dating Luminescence.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 2.5, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""OD (Ordnance Datum Newlyn)"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 1.33}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 1.56, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""WALIS Paleo RSL used as LITTORAL analytical elevation when available; measured indicator elevation preserved as reported observation.""}","[{""method"": ""luminescence"", ""relation"": ""equal"", ""age_ka"": 191.0, ""uncertainty_ka"": 19.0, ""material"": ""OSL"", ""notes"": ""WALIS reported age.""}]",1.56,1.56,1.56,1.56
f7568eea9c88d7e558a4d296acdc7c0b0bbbb290464dd1369d5e04eff80c999a,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,Morton,RSL_4063@row3432,52.95709,0.956835,reported,0.0,1.56,MSL,reported,raised_beach,Beach swash deposit,"[0.04999999999999993, 1.83]",184.0,luminescence,"Beach swash deposit; A sequence of deposits (overlying a basal till) largely made up of very well-sorted, predominantly subangular and subrounded fine quartz sands, with subsidiary feldspar and aragonite. The sands are characterized by approximately parallel bedding which dips seawards at low angles. This may represent swash cross-stratification typical of the swash zone of the foreshore. The presence of occasional gravels within the sands is also characteristic of deposits from this environment. The marginal marine origin of these units is supported by their very well-sorted particle-size distribution. The occurrence of aragonite within the mineral assemblage of sample 2 is suggestive of the presence of fragments of marine shell in the sands, although it is possible that the shells may have been reworked from older marine deposits.","Morton, Norfolk, Great Britain (UK)",Gale 1988 Hoare 2009 JQS,https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=3, age=4. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: SA-Morst-2. Analysis ID: 001. WALIS LUM ID: 505. Record Created by: Natasha Barlow. Last Update: 2021-06-21 15:14:53.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_4063@row3432"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_4063: Sea Level Indicator; Beach swash deposit; elevation 2.5 m; paleo RSL 1.56 m; dating Luminescence.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 2.5, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""OD (Ordnance Datum Newlyn)"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 1.33}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 1.56, ""deri