20d5b5f19baad248b1151e8189e6551292a85c1f386e35f66a228793d3f460df,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,Kikiakajik Beach - Beach,RSL_4168@row3449,70.03833,-22.24672,reported,0.00026556012729987867,9.63,MSL,reported,beachrock,Beach deposit or beachrock,"[-1.73, 1.9700000000000002]",132.0,luminescence,"Beach deposit or beachrock; Gravel foresets, intepreted to be a beach desposit, is part of a regressive sequence. Two exposures at this site were investigated. At one exposure, there were sublittoral bedded marine silts and sands up to an elevation of about 5.5 m. This unit contains warmer-than-present mollusc species, including Balanus crenatus and Astarte borealis. Above this is a coarser unit, with foreshore sand, and gravel forsets interpreted as beach deposits. The beach deposit contains lenses of silt with seaweed. The beach deposits were found between 6-7.5 m at one exposure, and 9-13 m at the second exposure. Overlying the beach unit is a diamiction interpreted as basal till from a Weichselian glacial advance.","Kikiakajik Beach, Beach, Ostgronland, Greenland","Mangerud and Funder, 1994 Mejdahl and Funder, 1994",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=3, age=4. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: R-931004. Analysis ID: ME94-003-001. WALIS LUM ID: 562. Record Created by: Evan Gowan. Last Update: 2021-10-21 01:58:04.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_4168@row3449"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_4168: Sea Level Indicator; Beach deposit or beachrock; elevation 9.75 m; paleo RSL 9.63 m; dating Luminescence.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 9.75, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 3.87}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 9.63, ""derived_depth_m"":