9c5f7d9a4f71e5b455f614decdc5004ef308382bd295fe0f2091bee7f8d3d7b7,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,"Cape Laundi, Sumba Island Reef Complex II (MIS 5e & 9) - Reef Complex II (MIS 5e & 9)",RSL_3593@row3581,-9.47655,120.185061,reported,3.077607292240311,41.05,unknown,reported,coral_reef,Coral reef terrace (general definition),"[-3.1950000000000003, -1.0850000000000002]",131.53,u_series,"Coral reef terrace (general definition); Elevation of highest dated sample at 40 m above MLWS with accuracy of ±5 m. The ages determined from the lower part of reef complex II (crests altitudes at ca. 50 m and 60m above MLWS) indicate a bimodal distribution: ages close to 130 ka belonging to MIS 5e and ages between 280 and 355 ka corresponding to MIS 9. Bard et al. (1996) found no MIS 7 corals in this reef complex. In earlier works (Pirazzoli et al., 1991 & 1993), Reef complex II formed during MIS 5, 7, 9.","Cape Laundi, Sumba Island Reef Complex II (MIS 5e & 9), Reef Complex II (MIS 5e & 9), Nusa Tenggara Timur, Indonesia","Bard et al., 1996 Pirazzoli et al., 1991b Pirazzoli et al., 1993 Maxwell et al., 2021 Chutcharavan and Dutton, 2020",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,0.955,"WALIS quality RSL=2, age=3. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=No. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS recalculated U-Series age. Originally reported ID: SBA22. Analysis ID: BR96-018-001. WALIS U-series ID: 1259. Record Created by: Kathrine Maxwell. Last Update: 2021-02-16 11:28:33.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_3593@row3581"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_3593: Sea Level Indicator; Coral reef terrace (general definition); elevation 38.91 m; paleo RSL 41.05 m; dating U-Series.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 38.91, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Low Water Springs (MLWS)"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 5.11}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevat