edbcee26d2c5393645650a80b158fbf03d5fb4bbadf9f1ced6181caa5dc10cf8,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,"Cape Namosain, Kupang, West Timor Terrace 5 (MIS 5e) - Terrace 5 (MIS 5e)",RSL_3614@row3609,-10.169737,123.547832,reported,0.0,44.28,MSL,reported,coral_reef,Coral reef terrace (general definition),"[-1.2349999999999999, -1.085]",152.0,u_series,"Coral reef terrace (general definition); ""Terrace 5, about 50 m wide on the transect, widens laterally up to 100 m; terrace 5 is the most distinctive terrace of the flight due to a prominent scarp up to 10-15 m high, itself incised by a deep notch. At the very Cape Namosain, where it reaches its maximum width, the terrace shows an internal lagoonal morphology. The front reef, which can then be compared to an external barrier reef, culminates at 44 m ALT, while the flat internal lagoon-like depression has an altitude of 40 m ALT.""","Cape Namosain, Kupang, West Timor Terrace 5 (MIS 5e), Terrace 5 (MIS 5e), Nusa Tenggara Timur, Indonesia","Jouannic et al., 1988 Maxwell et al., 2021",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=5, age=4. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=Yes. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: TM-TNU-5-1. Analysis ID: JO88-001-001. WALIS U-series ID: 2941. Record Created by: Kathrine Maxwell. Last Update: 2021-02-17 10:16:23.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_3614@row3609"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_3614: Sea Level Indicator; Coral reef terrace (general definition); elevation 43.12 m; paleo RSL 44.28 m; dating U-Series.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 43.12, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 0.4}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 44.28, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""WALIS Paleo RSL used as LITTORAL analy