ead879516806790975d239f183be9e1879cf9b239bb373bfaf3d4ad09d3ef1ac,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,"Cape Oeloimi, SE Semau Island, Kupang, W Lowest terrace (MIS 5e) - Lowest terrace (MIS 5e)",RSL_3615@row3610,-10.335544,123.400338,reported,0.0,8.43,MSL,reported,coral_reef,Coral reef terrace (general definition),"[-3.5, -1.12]",124.0,u_series,"Coral reef terrace (general definition); A 230Th/234U date of 124 ka±8 (TM-OLM-1-A-1) was obtained on a coral head collected in growth position on top of the youngest of four terraces at Cape Oeloimi, in the southeastern tip of the nearby island of Semau. Unlike the sub-horizontal series of Cape Namosain, the four terraces here are markedly tilted to the west, so that they successively intersect the south-facing coast of the cape, getting respectively older towards the west: the youngest reef rims the east-facing shoreline of Cape Oeloimi, with a maximum altitude of 7 m ALT in the southeasternmost part of the peninsula. Below this lowest emerged terrace, a very luxuriant modern platform is growing sub-horizontally, remaining submerged at low tide, like at Cape Namosain, but a little deeper (3-4 m deep).","Cape Oeloimi, SE Semau Island, Kupang, W Lowest terrace (MIS 5e), Lowest terrace (MIS 5e), Nusa Tenggara Timur, Indonesia","Jouannic et al., 1988 Maxwell et al., 2021",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=4, age=4. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=Yes. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: TM-OLM-1-A-1. Analysis ID: JO88-002-001. WALIS U-series ID: 2942. Record Created by: Kathrine Maxwell. Last Update: 2021-02-17 10:29:28.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_3615@row3610"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_3615: Sea Level Indicator; Coral reef terrace (general definition); elevation 6.12 m; paleo RSL 8.43 m; dating U-Series.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 6.12, ""reported_dept