5f3cd460e82ed3228dc0fec7166a5ef539a1646d9fbaf604e94ad07355e6cc3d,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,"Luwuk, Sulawesi Lower coral reef terrace (MIS 5a) - Lower coral reef terrace (MIS 5a)",RSL_3633@row3611,-0.94554,122.790052,reported,0.0,10.99,MSL,reported,coral_reef,Coral reef terrace (general definition),"[-9.995000000000001, -0.5049999999999999]",67.0,u_series,"Coral reef terrace (general definition); The Luwuk coast consists of coralline reef terraces rising stepwise from the present sea level to heights exceeding 400 m. The terraces may be divided into three groups: a lower, a middle and an upper group. In the vicinity of Luwuk the lower group consists of 6 distinct terraces that dip gently seaward (dip under 5°).","Luwuk, Sulawesi Lower coral reef terrace (MIS 5a), Lower coral reef terrace (MIS 5a), Sulawesi Tengah, Indonesia","Sumosusastro et al., 1989 Maxwell et al., 2021",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=2, age=4. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=Yes. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: G-88143. Analysis ID: SU89-003-001. WALIS U-series ID: 2913. Record Created by: Kathrine Maxwell. Last Update: 2021-02-17 10:51:34.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_3633@row3611"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_3633: Sea Level Indicator; Coral reef terrace (general definition); elevation 5.74 m; paleo RSL 10.99 m; dating U-Series.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 5.74, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 4.88}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 10.99, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""WALIS Paleo RSL used as LITTORAL analytical elevation when available; measured indicator elevation preserved as reported observation.""}","[{""method"": ""u_series"", ""relation"": ""eq