2b47dd55da3f66ded3dd87ef01eb6d0fd5ae1eab3aaa8b5e1a3343621a571b31,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,Rosh Hanikra SB - SB,RSL_928@row3619,33.093,35.105,reported,0.0,1.2,unknown,reported,raised_beach,Beach swash deposit,"[0.0, 0.14]","[115.0, 130.0]",u_series,"Beach swash deposit; The whole unit (Yasaf) is younger than MIS7 based on one OSL age obtained for the top of the underlying sandstone unit (Regba), dated in RHN to 215 ± 22ka. The Strombus unit overlying the Regba unit, was dated by U-Th. Fragments of 3 Strombuses divided to sub fragments were found recrystallized to calcite. The average age of ~110 ± 8 ka indicates diagenesis (shortly after the sea level retreat) under meteoric water, and therefore, falling RSL. Based on these two constrains the Strombus unit is younger than MIS7 and older than ~110 ± 8 ka","Rosh Hanikra SB, SB, The North, Israel","Sivan et al., 2016 Sisma Ventura et al., 2017 Sivan et al., 1999 Sivan and Galili, 2020",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=4, age=3. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS stratigraphic upper/lower age bounds. Originally reported ID: RH-S-1.1 A. Analysis ID: SI16-001. WALIS U-series ID: 1997. Record Created by: Dorit Sivan and Ehud Galili. Last Update: 2020-10-15 11:12:03.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_928@row3619"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_928: Sea Level Indicator; Beach swash deposit; elevation 1.27 m; paleo RSL 1.2 m; dating U-Series.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 1.27, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""ILSD"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 0.48}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 1.2, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""WALIS Paleo RSL used as LITTORAL analytical elevation when available; measured indicator elevation preserved as reported observation.""}","[{""m