3c914f57586edf745f5010340f201859d5dcb05003039d62d263bf2d92e0c6c5,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,240-S8 Milano Marittima Core S8 drilled NW of the town of Milano Marittima. Ground surface at +1.0 m asl. - Core S8 drilled NW of the town of Milano Marittima. Ground surface at +1.0 m asl.,RSL_1308@row3658,44.287225,12.326817,reported,0.0,-117.0,MSL,reported,raised_beach,Beach ridge,"[-10.0, 10.0]",129.0,esr,"Beach ridge; In the core from 128 to 118 m of depth the deposits correspond to teh coastal wedge formed during the Tyrrhenian transgression and consisting of sandy sediments in beach facies, from subtidal to beach ridge. According to Amorosi et al. (2004) between 118 and 105 m of depth also the MIS 5d and MIS 5c are reocrded, but they are documented as alluvial plain facies. The core is a reference for northern Adriatic stratigraphy as it has been investigated in detail for pollen sequence and the age has been checked also with an ESR date at the top of the beach sequence.","240-S8 Milano Marittima Core S8 drilled NW of the town of Milano Marittima. Ground surface at +1.0 m asl., Core S8 drilled NW of the town of Milano Marittima. Ground surface at +1.0 m asl., Emilia-Romagna, Italy","Ferranti et al., 2006 Amorosi et al., 2004 Campo et al., 2020 Cerrone et al., 2021",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=3, age=5. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: K-4384. Analysis ID: FE06-002-001. WALIS ESR ID: 134. Record Created by: Alessandro Fontana. Last Update: 2020-10-31 08:28:45.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_1308@row3658"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_1308: Sea Level Indicator; Beach ridge; elevation -117.0 m; paleo RSL -117.0 m; dating ESR.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": -117.0, ""reported_depth_m"": 117.0, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"",