2dc071de0d424413da131245d33d8e630ae73a2da4612b28cfd1d7b9c71d6f7e,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,One Tree Point type section - type section,RSL_34@row5166,-35.82201,174.45033,reported,0.002922641277802404,3.95,MSL,reported,raised_beach,Beach swash deposit,"[0.0, 1.3]",115.0,luminescence,"Beach swash deposit; Heavy mineral bed at the contact between foredune (Facies 3) and beach (Facies 2) facies, interpreted as a high tide swash deposit. The contact is exposed (and traced for 3.4 km) within a cliff providing a cross-section through a sequence of 20 relict beach ridges revealing well-preserved sedimentary structures and stratigraphic surfaces of nearshore, beach, and dune facies. The sequence is interpreted to record coastal progradation under a marine-dominated sand supply and assumed falling relative sea level. The elevation of the contact at the type section is described here. However, a plot of contact elevation exposed along the cliff section is shown in Figure 5 of the paper.","One Tree Point type section, type section, Northland, New Zealand (Aotearoa)","Nichol, 2002 Ryan et al., 2020",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=5, age=5. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: OTP1. Analysis ID: NI02-001-001. WALIS LUM ID: 1. Record Created by: Deirdre Ryan. Last Update: 2021-02-18 14:11:27.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_34@row5166"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_34: Sea Level Indicator; Beach swash deposit; elevation 4.6 m; paleo RSL 3.95 m; dating Luminescence.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 4.6, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 1.12}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 3.95, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""WALI