5d017bd3dd46ec89da51fc0b621f9adb9e509b43b48fd4c9910d6865d643e83c,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,Hicks Bay Otamaroa Terrace - Otamaroa Terrace,RSL_42@row5210,-37.59238,178.26899,reported,0.0,130.98,MSL,reported,marine_terrace,Marine Terrace,"[-2.145, 2.565]",68.7,luminescence,"Marine Terrace; Marine terrace located on the uplifting Raukumara Peninsula, North Island. Position of the section and sample on the terrace is not provided (inner, middle, outer margin). From terrace surface: non-marine coverbed thickness is 2.17 m overlying 2.5 m beach sands upon basement/shore platform. Proximity of the sands to the shoreline angle is unstated and there is no direct evidence of a beach depositional environment; however, the well-sorted nature of the sand and rounded gravels support wave sorting during deposition and this is considered a direct sea-level indicator from a marine terrace. No stratigraphic description for this site is provided in the GNS Online Data Repository.","Hicks Bay Otamaroa Terrace, Otamaroa Terrace, Gisborne, New Zealand (Aotearoa)","Wilson et al 2007 Iso et al 1982 Yoshikawa et al, 1980 Ryan et al., 2020",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,0.905,"WALIS quality RSL=2, age=1. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: HB-OT/WWL4 29. Analysis ID: WI07-005-001. WALIS LUM ID: 12. Record Created by: Deirdre Ryan. Last Update: 2021-02-18 14:24:15.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_42@row5210"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_42: Sea Level Indicator; Marine Terrace; elevation 131.2 m; paleo RSL 130.98 m; dating Luminescence.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 131.2, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 2.94}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 130.98, ""derived_d