1d846ad350f8c4382add43b21e6dceec4bc2d23aeddbf7a0ddcccd0195b52aa0,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,Omaio Otamaroa Terrace - Otamaroa Terrace,RSL_43@row5211,-37.7909,177.66962,reported,0.0,12.78,MSL,reported,marine_terrace,Marine Terrace,"[-2.145, 2.565]",64.5,luminescence,"Marine Terrace; The terrace is located on the uplifting Raukumara Peninsula, North Island. Position of the section and sample on the terrace is not provided (inner, middle, outer margin). From surface: non-marine coverbed thickness is 4 m overlying ~3 m beach sediments upon an irregular basement/shore platform contact. The beach sediments are subdivided into 2 m of medium bedded sand with gravel lenses overlying 1 m of rounded greywacked gravel (up to 100 mm diameter but averaging 20 mm diameter) within a coarse sand matrix. Proximity of the sands to the shoreline angle is unstated and there is no direct evidence of a beach depositional environment; however, the well-sorted nature of the sand and rounded gravels support wave sorting during deposition and this is considered a direct sea-level indicator from a marine terrace. Additional stratigraphic description for this site (stratigraphic column ID P10) is provided in the GNS Online Data Repository.","Omaio Otamaroa Terrace, Otamaroa Terrace, Bay of Plenty, New Zealand (Aotearoa)","Wilson et al 2007 Iso et al 1982 Yoshikawa et al, 1980 Ryan et al., 2020",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,0.905,"WALIS quality RSL=2, age=1. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: O-OT/WLL5 05. Analysis ID: WI07-002-001. WALIS LUM ID: 9. Record Created by: Deirdre Ryan. Last Update: 2021-03-08 12:00:31.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_43@row5211"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_43: Sea Level Indicator; Marine Terrace; elevation 13.0 m; paleo RSL 12.78 m; dating Luminescence.""}","{""reported_el