93b10c2a35e11c6a2f739bf4d09e47ca922b3c05603aa561485fe133762d9fb5,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,Blueskin Bay Warrington-2 - Warrington-2,RSL_49@row5220,-45.707466,170.603786,reported,0.0,1.15,MSL,reported,marine_terrace,Beach deposit or beachrock,"[-2.065, 1.7650000000000001]",97.0,luminescence,"Beach deposit or beachrock; A single 4-8 m high marine terrace slightly deformed, being tilted to the northeast and offset 1 m by a small northwest-striking fault. Quaternary volcanic boulder beach deposits are exposed and overlain by quartzofeldspathic beach sand. The beach boulders variably overlie shore platforms formed on loess or Miocene age volcanics. The beach sand is overlain by loess up to 5 m thick. The underlying loess unit crops out in multiple exposures and can be traced for 200-250 m southwards where it is overlain by Holocene deposits. The terrace has been traditionally correlated to MIS 5e based on elevation and would indicate tectonic stability since that time. Samples were taken from the underlying loess at Warrington-1 and from the beach sand at Warrington-2 c. 2.5 m, above contact with beach gravel. The beach sand is expected to approximate the age of the terrace, while the underlying loess should give maximum age for the terrace.","Blueskin Bay Warrington-2, Warrington-2, Otago, New Zealand (Aotearoa)","Litchfield and Lian, 2004 Barrell et al 1998 Rees-Jones et al 2000 Ryan et al., 2020",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,0.93,"WALIS quality RSL=1, age=3. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=blank. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: WBE2. Analysis ID: LI04-003-001. WALIS LUM ID: 26. Record Created by: Deirdre Ryan. Last Update: 2021-02-26 16:27:58.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_49@row5220"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_49: Sea Level Indicator; Beach deposit or beachrock; elevation 1.0 m; paleo RSL 1.15 m; dating Luminescence.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 1.0, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Mean Sea Level / General definition"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 2.43}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 1.15, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""WALIS Paleo RSL used as LITTORAL analytical elevation when available; measured indicator elevation preserved as reported observation.""}","[{""method"": ""luminescence"", ""relation"": ""equal"", ""age_ka"": 97.0, ""uncertainty_ka"": 11.0, ""material"": ""IRSL"", ""notes"": ""WALIS reported age.""}]",1.15,1.15,1.15,1.15
