4dbec8d6ced55d08171b38860d9691d8d8e89985cee760603ba659fd434d21af,walis_v1_0_post_review,sea_level_indicator,Coquille Point Whisky Run Terrace - Whisky Run Terrace,RSL_3477@row6310,43.114117,-124.437096,reported,0.36640470273516074,17.61,unknown,reported,marine_terrace,Marine Terrace,"[-3.15, 3.93]",72.7,u_series,"Marine Terrace; The Whiskey run terrace is the lowest in the sequence, and is a well preserved and regionally extensive. It is mantled by sediment varying in thickness from 2.5 to 20 m, which contains individual B. elegans. It is cut by a number of named faults. North of the Coquille river, the platform dips below sea level (potentially due to onshore extension of the Coquille fault), and south of the river it rises to present elevation and tilts seaward.","Coquille Point Whisky Run Terrace, Whisky Run Terrace, Oregon, United States of America","McInelly and Kelsey, 1990 Creveling et al., 2017 Griggs, 1945 Kennedy et al., 1982 Muhs et al., 1990 Muhs et al., 2006 Simms et al., 2016 Thompson and Creveling, 2021",https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5979520,1.0,"WALIS quality RSL=2, age=4. Originally accepted=Yes; accepted by other study=Yes. Elevation source: Paleo RSL (m). WALIS reported age. Originally reported ID: Kennedy Unidentified U-Series Sample. Analysis ID: KE82-001-001. WALIS U-series ID: 2406. Record Created by: Jessica Creveling and Schmitty Thompson. Last Update: 2021-06-22 16:02:15.","{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": ""WALIS Summary.csv"", ""section"": ""RSL_3477@row6310"", ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""WALIS row RSL_3477: Sea Level Indicator; Marine Terrace; elevation 18.0 m; paleo RSL 17.61 m; dating U-Series.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": 18.0, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": ""Not reported"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": 4.06}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 17.61, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""WALIS Paleo RSL used as LITTORAL analytical elev