9ac4c1dd5353752a55cb9507ad06b4a5a1df59e6e32906832ee7411b369528c6,blanchon2002,marine_limiting,Grand Cayman,mineru_llm_2_1,19.3298472,-81.1712216,inferred_text,10000.0,7.0,MSL,SRTM15+V2,guyot_or_drowned_platform,relic reef,null,null,other,Demise of the relic reef around Grand Cayman implies drowning due to rapid sea-level rises.,Grand Cayman,blanchon2002.pdf,https://doi.org/10.1016/S0037-0738(01)00143-9,0.63,Optional Ollama interpretation output. Geocoded from contextual query 'Grand Cayman'.,"{""page"": ""12"", ""figure"": ""Fig."", ""table"": null, ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""demise of the relic reef around Grand Cayman""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": null, ""reported_uncertainty_m"": null}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": 7.0, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 7.0, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""Elevation sampled from SRTM15+V2 at inferred coordinates because source elevation was not reported. Treat this as approximate spatial context, not a surveyed sample elevation.""}","[{""method"": ""other"", ""relation"": ""unknown"", ""age_ka"": null, ""uncertainty_ka"": null, ""material"": null, ""notes"": ""LLM-assisted extraction; raw BP-like numeric ages are normalized to ka.""}]",7,7,7,7
e2998227b6bc35ca88fa6311dde36a97ec7acbeef1cae6e0402f66983248d8cb,blanchon2002,sea_level_indicator,Narrative evidence locality,narrative_fallback_1,,,inferred_map,,-21.0,MSL,reported,marine_terrace,narrative fallback: submerged geomorphic sea-level feature,"[-23.5, -18.5]",8.1,stratigraphic_context,"marine terrace at Narrative evidence locality, reported around 21 m depth",Narrative evidence locality,Sedimentary Geology 147 (2002) 253 – 270,https://doi.org/10.1016/S0037-0738(01)00143-9,0.55,Narrative fallback cluster from prose description of submerged palaeolandscape; depth uncertainty widened pending human review.,"{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": null, ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""Abstract Drilling close to the base of a submerged sea-cliff on the terraced eastern shelf of Grand Cayman has revealed a relic Acropora palmata reef at a depth of 21 m below msl. Ten cores from its crest are principally composed of cobble-sized clasts of A. palmata set in a matrix of cemented skeletal grainstone. The clasts have a distinctive succession of encrusters that indicate rapid burial: a photophilic association of crustose coralline algae, foraminifera and vermetid gastropods superimposed by a cryptic association of sclerosponges, foraminifera and serpulids. In addition to rapid burial, U \u2013 Th thermal ionization mass spectrometer""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": 21.0, ""reported_datum"": ""MSL"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": null}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": null, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""Existing elevation preserved; no raster overwrite applied.""}","[{""method"": ""stratigraphic_context"", ""relation"": ""unknown"", ""age_ka"": 8.1, ""uncertainty_ka"": null, ""material"": null, ""notes"": ""Narrative fallback age context; review before analytical use.""}]",-21,-21,-21,-21
9118cd9a40173194319dc2b62cd5eed783e5dfd9e54afd9ce6f0c7d0fdbff340,blanchon2002,sea_level_indicator,Narrative evidence locality,narrative_fallback_2,,,inferred_map,,-21.0,MSL,reported,submerged_beach,narrative fallback: submerged geomorphic sea-level feature,"[-23.5, -18.5]",7.6,stratigraphic_context,"submerged beach at Narrative evidence locality, reported around 21 m depth",Narrative evidence locality,Sedimentary Geology 147 (2002) 253 – 270,https://doi.org/10.1016/S0037-0738(01)00143-9,0.55,Narrative fallback cluster from prose description of submerged palaeolandscape; depth uncertainty widened pending human review.,"{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": null, ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""e-generated terrestrial boulder ridges, which are easily confused with reef-crest deposits (e.g., Toscano and Lundberg, 1998). The age and elevation of the relic reef crest is consistent with the establishment of a 19-m shoreline between 8.1 and 7.6 ka on Grand Cayman (Blanchon and Jones, 1995). If we assume, as seems likely, that the 18.5-m intertidal notch on the west side of the island represents the actual sea level position (high tide), then the surface of the relic reef has been lowered 2 m from that level by marine erosion over the last 8 ka (i.e., an erosion rate of 0.25 mm year 1; cf. Acker and Risk, 1985). That assessment of erosion is not only supported by the presence of 1-m-deep erosional furrows cut into the present surface of the relic reef, but is also consistent with empir""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": 21.0, ""reported_datum"": ""MSL"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": null}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": null, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""Existing elevation preserved; no raster overwrite applied.""}","[{""method"": ""stratigraphic_context"", ""relation"": ""unknown"", ""age_ka"": 7.6, ""uncertainty_ka"": null, ""material"": null, ""notes"": ""Narrative fallback age context; review before analytical use.""}]",-21,-21,-21,-21
4dd0d96e6b133b79f90b4e816af9f374480b06178d2064eb03dae2bd9972d10a,bowen1991,sea_level_indicator,Easington Raised Beach,llm_feature_1,55.088,-1.737,inferred_map,,32,OD,other,raised_beach,gravel,null,"""Oxygen Isotope Stage 7 (200 ka)""","Amino acid geochronology (D/L ratios), Radiocarbon dating",Gravel of the Easington Raised Beach rests on a bevelled platform of Magnesian Limestone at about 32m above O.D. at the head of Shippersea Bay. It contains marine shells.,"Easington, County Durham","Bowen, D.Q., Smith, D.B., and Sykes, G.A. (1991). The age of the Easington Raised Beach, County Durham. Proceedings of the Yorkshire Geological Society, 48(Part 4), 415-420.",http://pygs.lyellcollection.org/,0.82,Amino acid D/L ratios correlated with the Minchin Hole Stage and Oxygen Isotope Stage 7. Reworked fauna suggests Stage 9. No contextual geocode result was found.,"{""page"": ""415-420"", ""figure"": ""1, 2, 3"", ""table"": ""1, 2"", ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""The gravel of the Easington Raised Beach rests on a bevelled platform of Magnesian Limestone at about 32m above O.D. at the head of Shippersea Bay, Easington.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": null, ""reported_uncertainty_m"": null}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": null, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""Existing elevation preserved; no raster overwrite applied.""}","[{""method"": ""Amino acid geochronology (D/L ratios), Radiocarbon dating"", ""relation"": ""unknown"", ""age_ka"": ""Oxygen Isotope Stage 7 (200 ka)"", ""uncertainty_ka"": null, ""material"": null, ""notes"": ""LLM-assisted extraction; raw BP-like numeric ages are normalized to ka.""}]",32,32,32,32
