27e878b7c28c5a5b4643a887d54a8653c6ba49871f9b3e6d16a2cf35afc1c9b4,gallagher2015,sea_level_indicator,"Fethard, The Municipal District of Carrick-on-Suir, County Tipperary, Munster, Éire / Ireland",heuristic_feature_1,52.467222,-7.691111,inferred_text,10000.0,64.0,MSL,SRTM15+V2,raised_beach,heuristically extracted from explicit text,null,null,other,"A Marine Isotope Stage 4 age for Pleistocene raised beach deposits near Fethard, southern Ireland","Fethard, The Municipal District of Carrick-on-Suir, County Tipperary, Munster, Éire / Ireland","A Marine Isotope Stage 4 age for Pleistocene raised beach deposits near Fethard, southern Ireland",https://doi.org/10.1002/jqs.2808,0.7,Extracted using heuristic parser from pdf text after methods: pdftotext. Place name geocoded from query 'Fethard'.,"{""page"": ""1-2"", ""figure"": null, ""table"": null, ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""artment of Geography, Durham University, Durham DH1 3LE, UK 1 Received 20 August 2014; Revised 27 August 2015; Accepted 6 September 2015 ABSTRACT: Raised beach deposits around the Irish coast have been interpreted as interglacial or last glacial in age. On the south coast of Ireland, the Courtmacsherry Formation raised beach (CFB), near Fethard, County Wexford, was dated using optically stimulated luminescence (OSL). This site was previously dated to Marine Isotope Stage (MIS) 6\u20135, but more recent dating of the CFB elsewhere along the south coast shows it is considerably younger (MIS 4\u20133).""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": null, ""reported_uncertainty_m"": null}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": 64.0, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 64.0, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""Elevation sampled from SRTM15+V2 at inferred coordinates because source elevation was not reported. Treat this as approximate spatial context, not a surveyed sample elevation.""}","[{""method"": ""other"", ""relation"": ""