6afd18d9a34c8473f5eba4ebdd734054529ba216d6100375ba3f9463539f6906,mchugh2010,sea_level_indicator,Narrative evidence locality,narrative_fallback_1,,,inferred_map,,-38.0,MSL,reported,submerged_beach,narrative fallback: submerged geomorphic sea-level feature,"[-40.5, -35.5]",6.0,stratigraphic_context,"submerged beach at Narrative evidence locality, reported around 38 m depth",Narrative evidence locality,"The role of glacio-eustasy in sequence formation: Mid-Atlantic Continental Margin, USA",https://doi.org/10.1016/j.margeo.2010.08.009,0.55,Narrative fallback cluster from prose description of submerged palaeolandscape; depth uncertainty widened pending human review.,"{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": null, ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""smic facies associated with the last major glaciation, and oxygen isotope stages OIS 5 to OIS 1 were examined and a chronology was constructed from mollusk assemblages of intertidal origin that allowed tracking the paleoshoreline from 19 to 6 ka BP. The maximum extent of the Last Glacial Maximum (LGM) paleoshoreline at 17 ka BP was documented near the 120 m modern isobath. The shoreline was marked by sediment mounds up to 5 m high and troughs 15 m deep and 1 km wide (interpreted as shoreface and tidal inlet or lagoons) formed from 17 to 15 ka BP. Five kilometers seaward from the LGM shoreline and the head of the Hudson Canyon is a wedge-shaped feature interpreted as a lowstand delta. Sediments older than the last glacial, possibly OIS 3 or OIS 5, onlap a basal unconformity. We correlate th""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": 38.0, ""reported_datum"": ""MSL"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": null}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": null, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""Existing elevation preserved; no raster overwrite applied.""}","[{""method"": ""stratigraphic_context"", ""relation"": ""unknown"", ""age_ka"": 6.0, ""uncertainty_ka"": null, ""material"": null, ""notes"": ""Narrative fallback age context; review before analytical use.""}]",-38,-38,-38,-38
78ec4b71fc38f4c543413bebb86817c649a3fc0637d69eb634fb7dd79e5eea8f,mchugh2010,sea_level_indicator,Narrative evidence locality,narrative_fallback_2,,,inferred_map,,-120.0,MSL,reported,submerged_beach,narrative fallback: submerged geomorphic sea-level feature,"[-122.5, -117.5]","""Holocene""",stratigraphic_context,"submerged beach at Narrative evidence locality, reported around 120 m depth",Narrative evidence locality,"The role of glacio-eustasy in sequence formation: Mid-Atlantic Continental Margin, USA",https://doi.org/10.1016/j.margeo.2010.08.009,0.55,Narrative fallback cluster from prose description of submerged palaeolandscape; depth uncertainty widened pending human review.,"{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": null, ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""k gray (2.5Y 4/1) and gray brown (2.5Y 5/2). Grayish brown (2.5Y 4/2) sand laminae and beds are also present. The \ufb01ne-grained sediments and rare shell fragments indicate that Facies 4a was deposited distal from the paleoshoreline. CHIRP pro\ufb01les show that Facies 4a is associated with seismic re\ufb02ections that are acoustically strati\ufb01ed and parallel to the sea \ufb02oor and were deposited above of\ufb02ap surface p(0). This indicates a relative age younger than the last glacial. Interpretation: Holocene drape. Facies 4b Interbedded color banded mud, sandy mud, and very \ufb01negrained quartz sand and glauconitic sand laminae (Fig. 3A). The mud is gray (5Y 5/1), commonly stained with hydrotroilite, and color banded: pale red (10R 6/2; 2.5 YR6/2); light gray (10YR 7/1); dark gray (5Y 4/1); olive gray""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": 120.0, ""reported_datum"": ""MSL"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": null}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": null, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""Existing elevation preserved; no raster overwrite applied.""}","[{""method"": ""stratigraphic_context"", ""relati