5fd001ddab8e986ddf16075194d7885eafbdeb35925ecb76479743d65d793c70,reid1929,sea_level_indicator,Balnakiel Raised Beach,llm_feature_1,,,inferred_map,,null,unknown,other,raised_beach,Cemented sand / Shore sand,null,null,other,"Raised beach consisting of cemented sand in a half-saucer-like depression. The cemented mass is divided into four zones: dolomite fragments, rounded pebbles, quartz sand (max 5 inches), and dolomitic pebbles. Found in Durness Dolomites sea-wall.","Southern shore of Bahnakiel Bay (Bagh Baille-na-Cille), near Durness, Sutherlandshire","Reid, D. M. (1929). 'On a Raised Beach on the North Coast of Scotland'.",,0.37,Contains burrows of marine annelid and fragments of molluscan shells. Line of demarcation coincides with a fault. Mechanical analysis matches typical shore sand from Beinne Ceannabeinne. No contextual geocode result was found.,"{""page"": """", ""figure"": ""Fig. 1, Fig. 2"", ""table"": ""Mechanical analysis of sand (silt, F.S., M.S., C.S. percentages)"", ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""The area in which occurs the raised beach about to be described forms the southern shore of Bahnakiel Bay... there is a half-saucer-like depression in the cliff top... In the landward part of the depression is to be found the really conclusive evidence of the old sea beach in the form of \u201ccemented sand\u201d... This beach, standing as it does about 25 feet above sea-level, obviously belongs to the lowest group of raised beaches.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": null, ""reported_uncertainty_m"": null}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": null, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""No coordinates available for DEM elevation sampling.""}","[{""method"": ""other"", ""relation"": ""unknown"", ""age_ka"": null, ""uncertainty_ka"": null, ""material"": null, ""notes"": ""LLM-assisted extraction; raw BP-like numeric ages are normalized to ka.""}]",,,,
