e91fc4a3e13584ae5261cbef345f7e1ae21eb3c59f49628191ce22e2e1f5ad21,desantis2014,sea_level_indicator,Coppa Nevigata,llm_feature_1,41.558074,15.8338518,inferred_text,10000.0,0.0,MSL,SRTM15+V2,marine_terrace,llm-extracted candidate,null,"""MIS 11""",AAR,"A Middle Pleistocene marine terrace deposit (NVI unit) consisting of tawny/yellow sand and clayey silt, rich in stromatolites and marine shells, interpreted as a brackish lagoon.","Manfredonian Gulf, Gargano headland, Apulia","De Santis, V., Caldara, M., Torres, T., & Ortiz, J. E. (2014). Two middle Pleistocene warm stages in the terrace deposits of the Apulia region (southern Italy). Quaternary International, 332, 2-18.",https://doi.org/10.1016/j.quaint.2013.10.009,0.85,"The site is located at approximately 7 m above present sea level. The unit is assigned to MIS 11. Geocoded from contextual query 'Coppa Nevigata, Apulia, Italy'.","{""page"": ""6"", ""figure"": ""4"", ""table"": ""1"", ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""At Coppa Nevigata, the NVI unit is composed of tawny or yellow ochre sand with rare polygenic centimetric pebbles. The sand grades upwards into light yellow and ochre sandy/clayey silt or clay. Some layers are cemented and form marly limestones which contains columnar stromatolites.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": null, ""reported_uncertainty_m"": null}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": 0.0, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 0.0, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""Elevation sampled from SRTM15+V2 at inferred coordinates because source elevation was not reported. Treat this as approximate spatial context, not a surveyed sample elevation.""}","[{""method"": ""AAR"", ""relation"": ""unknown"", ""age_ka"": ""MIS 11"", ""uncertainty_ka"": null, ""material"": null, ""notes"": ""LLM-assisted extraction; raw BP-like numeric ages are normalized to ka.""}]",0,0,0,0
2642b7865911ced60faa6bd2d29cc3325d8ff4616ee5466b0c8bbe5611183628,desantis2014,sea_level_indicator,Trani cliff,llm_feature_2,41.264444,16.444444,reported,,12.0,MSL,SRTM15+V2,marine_terrace,llm-extracted candidate,null,"""MIS 9""",AAR,"A Middle Pleistocene marine terrace deposit (Unit I) consisting of cemented limestone, porous bioconstructed bodies with Characeae, and calcarenite layers, interpreted as a hypersaline-brackish lagoon.","Apulia, Italy","De Santis, V., Caldara, M., Torres, T., & Ortiz, J. E. (2014). Two middle Pleistocene warm stages in the terrace deposits of the Apulia region (southern Italy). Quaternary International, 332, 2-18.",https://doi.org/10.1016/j.quaint.2013.10.009,0.9,The cliff is approximately 10 m high. The unit is assigned to MIS 9. No contextual geocode result was found.,"{""page"": ""6"", ""figure"": ""4"", ""table"": ""1"", ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""At the Trani cliff, Unit I consists of cemented, whitish, fine-grained, massive or bedded limestone. The limestone grades upwards into massive, porous bioconstructed calcareous bodies composed of in situ Charophyta stems and/or stromatolites.""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": null, ""reported_datum"": null, ""reported_uncertainty_m"": null}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": 12.0, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": 12.0, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""Elevation sampled from SRTM15+V2 at authoritative coordinates because source elevation was not reported.""}","[{""method"": ""AAR"", ""relation"": ""unknown"", ""age_ka"": ""MIS 9"", ""uncertainty_ka"": null, ""material"": null, ""notes"": ""LLM-assisted extraction; raw BP-like numeric ages are normalized to ka.""}]",12,12,12,12
61788442327af4d5f153db99affd69e7aade52171f5af72d8edd33fa79075fd4,desantis2014,sea_level_indicator,Narrative evidence locality,narrative_fallback_1,,,inferred_map,,-10.0,MSL,reported,marine_terrace,narrative fallback: submerged geomorphic sea-level feature,"[-12.5, -7.5]",500.0,stratigraphic_context,"marine terrace at Narrative evidence locality, reported around 10 m depth",Narrative evidence locality,Two middle Pleistocene warm stages in the terrace deposits of the Apulia region (southern Italy),https://doi.org/10.1016/j.quaint.2013.10.009,0.55,Narrative fallback cluster from prose description of submerged palaeolandscape; depth uncertainty widened pending human review.,"{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": null, ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""tion (Hoffmann et al., 2007). In the Mediterranean area, deposits that are correlated with MIS 11 and MIS 9 are rare and poorly documented. On the Tyrrhenian coast of south Calabria (Italy), Miyauchi et al. (1994) dated terrace VII, which is 140e430 m a.s.l., at MIS 9 or 11 based on foraminifera, nannoplankton analysis, and the occurrence of \u201cminor\u201d Senegalese fauna. Zazo et al. (2003) assigned two marine terraced deposits of Cala Blava and Cape Orenol (Mallorca Island, Spain) to MIS 11 or possibly MIS 9 based on dating of underlying units and/or their elevations above the present sea level. Both units, which are located at 10 m a.s.l., consist of well-cemented conglomerate that is 0.5 m thick and contains marine bioclasts and warm faunas (Senegalese fauna). Karner and Marra (2003) dated t""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": 10.0, ""reported_datum"": ""MSL"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": null}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": null, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""Existing elevation preserved; no raster overwrite applied.""}","[{""method"": ""stratigraphic_context"", ""relation"": ""unknown"", ""a