6ed4ba586fa300c58488f5b1ffa8ed72a29f0d54bba4afea130e3c7ec36ac019,desantis2014,sea_level_indicator,Narrative evidence locality,narrative_fallback_2,,,inferred_map,,-32.0,MSL,reported,marine_terrace,narrative fallback: submerged geomorphic sea-level feature,"[-34.5, -29.5]","""Pleistocene""",stratigraphic_context,"marine terrace at Narrative evidence locality, reported around 32 m depth",Narrative evidence locality,Two middle Pleistocene warm stages in the terrace deposits of the Apulia region (southern Italy),https://doi.org/10.1016/j.quaint.2013.10.009,0.55,Narrative fallback cluster from prose description of submerged palaeolandscape; depth uncertainty widened pending human review.,"{""page"": null, ""figure"": null, ""table"": null, ""section"": null, ""quote_or_paraphrase"": ""I may be related to MIS 11 and 9, respectively, based on their elevations and some 230Th/234U dates obtained for Units III and IV, which lie on the lowest platform (III). Santoro et al. (2009) studied the raised coastal terraces along the Ionian Sea coast of northern Calabria (Italy) and speculated that the highest terraces (T9 to T11) may represent MIS 15e11 or 11e9. Antonioli et al. (1988) and Antonioli (2012) described fossiliferous yellow-ochre sands at a depth of 32 m b.s.l. in a core drilled in the Fondi plain. The depositional environments of the sands range from a brackish environment at the base to a marine environment in the middle to a continental environment at the top. These sands have been dated using amino acid racemisation (AAR) to aminozone G (MIS 9). In the Apulia region""}","{""reported_elevation_m"": null, ""reported_depth_m"": 32.0, ""reported_datum"": ""MSL"", ""reported_uncertainty_m"": null}","{""raw_raster_value_m"": null, ""applied_correction_m"": null, ""derived_elevation_m"": null, ""derived_depth_m"": null, ""derivation_notes"": ""Existing elevation preserved; no raster overwrite applied.""}","[{""method"": ""stratigraphic_context"", ""relation"": ""unknown"", ""age_ka"": ""Pleistocene"", ""uncertainty_ka"": null, ""material"": null, ""notes"": ""Narrative fallback age context; review before analytical use.""}]",-32,-32,-32,-32
